# Walkthrough - Admin Inventory Management Links

I have successfully replaced the administrative "Import Tool" links with direct "Manage Inventory" buttons across all four TCG categories on the public store pages. These links are **only visible to admins**.

## Changes Made

### 🎴 Lorcana
- **Index Page**: Removed the "Open Import Tool" link. Admins now see a **Manage Lorcana Inventory** button.
- **Set Page**: Added a **Manage Lorcana Inventory** button when a set has no stocked cards.

### 🪄 Magic: The Gathering
- **Index Page**: Admins now see a **Manage Magic Inventory** button if the set list is empty.
- **Set Page**: Added a **Manage Magic Inventory** button for admins when an individual set has no stock.

### 🏴‍☠️ One Piece
- **Index Page**: Admins now see a **Manage One Piece Inventory** button if the set list is empty.
- **Set Page**: Added a **Manage One Piece Inventory** button for admins when an individual set has no stock.

### 🐹 Pokémon
- **Index Page**: Admins now see a **Manage Pokémon Inventory** button if the set list is empty.
- **Set Page**: Added a **Manage Pokémon Inventory** button for admins when an individual set has no stock.

## Visual Verification
The new buttons follow the premium store aesthetic and use category-specific icons (boxes, pirate flag, etc.).

> [!NOTE]
> These buttons will only appear if the logged-in account has `is_admin = 1`. Regular customers will still see the standard "Cards are being priced" or "Back to Store" messages.

## Verification
- Verified that the links point to the correct administrative URL endpoints (e.g., `Admin/lorcana_inventory`).
- Verified that the logic checks the session's admin status before rendering the buttons.
